            <ArticleTitle>The use of iatrogenic hypothyroidism to treat intractable angina.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>285-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>An elderly man who had incapacitating angina, despite coronary artery surgery and maximal medical management was deliberately made hypothyroid with radio-iodine. Five years later he was virtually free of chest pain. There is still a limited number of patients in whom this is a useful form of therapy, despite the attendant morbidity of myxoedema.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
